-- title:
--   Supersingular points of the full-level chart are separated by prime-to-q level
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field over $\mathbb Q$, write $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\pi_0\in k_0$ have image in $A$; assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell'\ne q$, $\ell'\ge 3$, $\ell'\nmid M'$, let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity admitting a ring embedding $k_0\to\mathbb C$ carrying it to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K\subseteq k_0((\mathfrak q))$ be `laurentBaseChange` of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times\bigr)$, an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`; let $K''$ be the analogous field at level $\ell'^2M'$ with $H''=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/\ell'^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell')^\times\bigr)$. Let $y_1,y_2$ be maximal ideals of the $A_0$-subalgebra $C':=$ `chartAlgFin` $A_0\,K\,j$ of $K$, both containing the image of $\pi_0$, and assume: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C'\to\Omega$ with kernel $y_1$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet` $q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point; and for every $x\in C'$ whose Laurent series is $\mathfrak q\mapsto\mathfrak q^{q}$ substituted into (that is, `qExpand` $k_0\,q$ applied to) the Laurent series of some $g\in K''$, one has $x\in y_1\iff x\in y_2$. Then $y_1=y_2$.
--
--   This is the statement that a supersingular closed point of the special fibre of the integral model at full level $(q\ell')^2M'$ is determined by the prime-to-$q$ level data: the degeneracy copy of the level-$\ell'^2M'$ function field obtained by $\mathfrak q\mapsto\mathfrak q^{q}$ separates points, because over a supersingular $j$-invariant the level-$q$ structure degenerates. It feeds the reduction analysis in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin).
